Comment: CRITICAL: This is a STUB PLACEHOLDER — not a valid GPG key.
Comment:
Comment: The actual signing key for SHA256SUMS.asc is NOT bundled in this repository.
Comment: Reason: Ansible Galaxy does not publish GPG signatures or SLSA provenance for
Comment:         community collections. Without upstream-signed artifacts, this project
Comment:         cannot establish a chain of trust to a maintainer public key.
Comment:
Comment: Current Verification Model:
Comment:   - SHA256SUMS is committed to git but is NOT GPG-signed by a real key
Comment:   - verify-collections.sh validates GPG signatures when keys are available (advisory)
Comment:   - Bootstrap and CI verify hashes against Galaxy API and upstream GitHub sources
Comment:   - Primary defense: MANDATORY CODE REVIEW of collection upgrades before merge
Comment:   - Secondary defense: CI re-verifies against Galaxy API post-commit (detects drift)
Comment:
Comment: To enable real GPG verification:
Comment:   1. Obtain the Ansible collections maintainer public key via keyserver:
Comment:      gpg --keyserver keys.openpgp.org --recv-keys AE97E86A1C807F5FA6A7987B68B6396B4E11D882
Comment:   2. Verify the fingerprint matches the documented value in SECURITY.md
Comment:   3. After import, GPG signature checks in verify-collections.sh will work
Comment:
Comment: See SECURITY.md § "Ansible Collections Supply Chain" for complete details,
Comment: mitigation strategies, and future plans for SLSA provenance verification.

